Then we will put in our O, our C
double bond O, as well as, and I'm

00:16:01.204 --> 00:16:06.665
going to just kind of emphasize
that O minus with an Na plus, right?

00:16:06.785 --> 00:16:09.435
So that's what makes our salt compound.

00:16:10.064 --> 00:16:13.064
Now the other portion is
going to be an alcohol.

00:16:13.714 --> 00:16:19.315
So we'll have our h o attached to
being that this is a one member

00:16:19.315 --> 00:16:24.255
chain, so it'd be the H three
oh or also known as methanol.

